      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ve got a thought today that maybe these two variants would suffice here. Since capability fields carry their own type, the type of the range does not necessarily need to be of the same type. The two things we care about when defining a range are the span and the allowed precision. Thus, a \"long\" range will cover all integer cases, and \"float\" will cover all float cases. For example, we still can use \"long\" range type when defining a range for an integer capability.",
